   "widgets_values": [
    "YouTube tutorial from real Hanzo screens.\n\n1  Script: HanzoChat writes the narration from the brief in its prompt (edit the brief, keep the shape).\n2  Voiceover: HanzoTTS speaks it. 3  Music: HanzoMusic makes the bed.\n4  Screens: LoadImage takes real captures from hanzo.ai's public/shots and public/templates; RepeatImageBatch holds each for its seconds \u00d7 30.\n5  CreateVideo joins the screens with the voiceover; SaveVideo writes the MP4.\n\nFor typed prompts, cursor moves, card count-ups and burned-in captions over these same screens, render the HyperFrames project instead (videos/hanzo-first-1000: npx hyperframes render). This graph is the one-click version: real screens, real voice, one file."
   ],
   "title": "How this works"
  }
